## Example UI Test App

```dart
// api_test_app.dart - Run with: flutter run -d chrome api_test_app.dart

import 'package:flutter/material.dart';
import 'package:your_app/repository/your_repository.dart';

void main() {
  runApp(const ApiTestApp());
}

class ApiTestApp extends StatelessWidget {
  const ApiTestApp({Key? key}) : super(key: key);

  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) {
    return MaterialApp(
      debugShowCheckedModeBanner: false,
      theme: ThemeData(
        useMaterial3: true,
        colorScheme: ColorScheme.fromSeed(seedColor: Colors.blue),
      ),
      home: const ApiTestScreen(),
    );
  }
}

class ApiTestScreen extends StatefulWidget {
  const ApiTestScreen({Key? key}) : super(key: key);

  @override
  State<ApiTestScreen> createState() => _ApiTestScreenState();
}

class _ApiTestScreenState extends State<ApiTestScreen> {
  final _repo = YourRepository();
  String _result = 'Results will appear here';
  bool _isLoading = false;

  Future<void> _testApiCall() async {
    setState(() {
      _isLoading = true;
      _result = 'Testing API...';
    });

    try {
      // Replace with your actual repository call
      final result = await _repo.yourApiMethod(
        param1: 'value1',
        param2: 'value2',
      );

      // Format and display the result
      setState(() {
        _result = 'SUCCESS!\n${result.toString()}';
      });
    } catch (e) {
      setState(() {
        _result = 'ERROR: $e';
      });
    } finally {
      setState(() {
        _isLoading = false;
      });
    }
  }

  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) {
    return Scaffold(
      appBar: AppBar(
        title: const Text('API Test'),
        centerTitle: true,
      ),
      body: Padding(
        padding: const EdgeInsets.all(16.0),
        child: Column(
          crossAxisAlignment: CrossAxisAlignment.stretch,
          children: [
            ElevatedButton(
              onPressed: _isLoading ? null : _testApiCall,
              child: Text(_isLoading ? 'Testing...' : 'Test API Call'),
            ),
            const SizedBox(height: 20),
            const Text(
              'API Response:',
              style: TextStyle(fontWeight: FontWeight.bold),
            ),
            const SizedBox(height: 8),
            Expanded(
              child: Container(
                padding: const EdgeInsets.all(12),
                decoration: BoxDecoration(
                  border: Border.all(color: Colors.grey),
                  borderRadius: BorderRadius.circular(8),
                ),
                child: SingleChildScrollView(
                  child: Text(_result),
                ),
              ),
            ),
          ],
        ),
      ),
    );
  }
}
```

## Replacement Test Values

When testing API repositories, use these standard test values that won't affect production data:

| Parameter      | Test Value   | Description                         |
|----------------|--------------|-------------------------------------|
| restaurantId   | "rest001"    | Test restaurant identifier          |
| tableId        | "table001"   | Test table identifier               |
| sessionId      | "session001" | Test session identifier             |
| orderId        | "order001"   | Test order identifier               |
| customerId     | "cust001"    | Test customer identifier            |
| productId      | "prod001"    | Test product identifier             |
| quantity       | 1            | Test quantity                       |
| notes          | "Test notes" | Test notes for orders               |

## Handling Repository Dependencies

If your repository depends on services or other dependencies, you have several options:

1. **Direct instantiation**: Create the dependencies directly in your test
2. **Dependency replacement**: Create mock or fake implementations for testing
3. **GetIt overrides**: Override GetIt registrations for testing if your app uses GetIt 
4. **Provider overrides**: Use Provider.value to provide test implementations

Always prefer the simplest approach for quick testing.